{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDING HAZARD — this change must NOT land before the store actually works. Plan review\ncaught a factual error in my safety argument and it turns out to matter operationally.\n\nI wrote: 'the production box today sets no tracker dir, so expected is false, so the gate is\nINERT and cannot refuse a healthy container.' That was TRUE when written and became FALSE when\nkilted-nuclear-bronco (Gerrit 2231) merged and deployed — that change sets\nREBAR_TRACKER_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets on the mcp service. Verified on the live\ncontainer just now:\n\n    REBAR_TRACKER_DIR on the live container: /var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets   -> expected = TRUE\n    store present?                            NO                            -> present  = FALSE\n\nThat is precisely the gate's refusal condition. If this change deployed today the readiness gate\nwould refuse to promote EVERY mcp container with mcp-store-missing, blocking all mcp deploys\nuntil the store is repaired. The gate would be doing exactly what it was designed to do; the\nmistake is mine, in reasoning about inertness from a premise that a sibling change had already\ninvalidated.\n\nCONSEQUENCE, recorded as a dependency: this ticket now depends_on fathomable-yester-thrip (the\npoisoned-volume fix, Gerrit 2244). The store on the box is currently a 1.5GB partial clone with\nno resolvable HEAD; until a real clone lands, expected=true/present=false is the steady state\nand this gate must not go live.\n\nThe gate logic itself is unchanged and correct — keying on expected AND NOT present is still the\nright condition, and the three harness tests still pass. What changed is only WHEN it is safe to\nenable, and that is now enforced by the link rather than by a paragraph."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787759821651025001,"uuid":"9778abeb-052b-4713-b4b5-e778c8e1191b"}